<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Calpixque</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The calpixque (singular calpixqui) were the tribute collectors and regional administrators of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>. They collected tribute from subject provinces, maintained order and reported to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>. They formed an important link between the imperial centre and the conquered city-states.</p></div>
